  "body": "## What changed\n\nA pocket-family operation (2D Pocket, 2D Adaptive, 2D Offset) can clear the stock around the part. This occurs with a whole-model source (#12), or with the stock source when the setup holds parts (#1554). Before this fix, such an operation gave no pass to a band of that area narrower than the tool, and it gave no note. The outside of the part stayed uncut and nothing told the user.\n\nNow the operation carries one note for those bands. The note gives:\n\n- the operation kind,\n- the tool diameter and the stock to leave,\n- the XY box of each band,\n- what to do: use a smaller tool, or a wider stock margin.\n\nExample: `2D Adaptive: 1 band of the area to clear is narrower than the 10.000 mm tool, so no pass cuts it: X -35.000 mm to 35.000 mm, Y -35.000 mm to 35.000 mm - use a smaller tool, or a wider stock margin`\n\nThe cut does not change. A region where the tool reaches every piece gets no note, so no golden changes.\n\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/unreached.rs` (new): `unreached_pieces` and `unreached_note`. These pure functions find each connected piece of the region that erodes to nothing by the tool radius plus the stock to leave. They ignore noise slivers (narrower than 0.01 mm, or smaller than 1e-4 mm^2).\n- `crates/app/src/operation/keep_law.rs`: `narrow_noted` adds the note for the pocket family only, and only when the operation clears around the part. The note never blocks the cut. If the band check cannot read the region, the path stays and a note says that the check did not run.\n- `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs`: one call after generation.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/1655-narrow-band-note.md`. A note is used, not a cut past the stock edge. A cut past the stock edge would move every around-part pocket and its goldens. A follow-up issue can cut the band.\n\n## Cause\n\n`machining2d::pocket_entered` erodes the region by the tool radius plus the stock to leave. It refuses only a region that erodes to nothing as a whole. A connected piece that erodes to nothing gets no pass, and nothing reported it.\n\n## How tested\n\nPinning tests:\n\n- `crates/app/tests/narrow_band.rs`\n  - `a_model_source_adaptive_names_the_outside_band_narrower_than_the_tool`: a 3 mm margin with a 10 mm tool. 2D Adaptive and 2D Pocket, with the part source and the stock source. The pocket in the part is cut, no pass is in the band, and one note names the band box.\n  - `a_band_the_tool_fits_is_cut_and_says_nothing`: an 11 mm margin. The band is cut and no note is given.\n- `camcraft-motion` unit tests `machining2d::unreached::law::*`: a band beside a wide bore, the stock to leave in the reach, a noise sliver, an empty region and a NaN reach.\n\nQuick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` plan, run with `-j 4`): the motion suites and the app suites in the plan. Also `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`. Results: all motion suites pass; the app suites pass except `lead_approach` (2 tests). That suite fails the same way on the base without this change: it is #1675 (main is red after #1656). Clippy is clean. After a last edit (the note never blocks the cut), `narrow_band`, `keep_law` and `stock_source_law` ran again and pass.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A 3+2 tilted setup frame. The note box is in the local frame of the operation.\n- Inch units (the format uses the same `units::len` path as the other notes).\n- 2D Offset and the trochoidal method of 2D Adaptive: they use the same call site, but no test names them.\n- The GUI. The note shows where the other operation notes show.\n\nChangelog: A 2D Pocket, Adaptive or Offset that clears the stock around a part now names each band of the stock narrower than the tool, which no pass can cut (#1655)\n\nEffort: high\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #1655\n",
